## Context

The ratified target-neutral harness includes `54yyyu/zotero-mcp` alongside
zoteus. Both are external servers using Zotero's local API, so this target asks
whether the interface transports between independent implementations of the
same architecture class rather than only across classes.

## Actions

1. Pin the tested zotero-mcp revision and reproducible default setup.
2. Declare derived state, query transport, process lifecycle, default
   configuration and unsupported interface verbs.
3. Add only minimal transport code, with no option or access unavailable to an
   ordinary user, and run the shared assertions unchanged.
4. Compare adapter declarations rather than target behavior with zoteus to
   identify accidental coupling in the interface.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] pinned zotero-mcp revision and reproducible target setup
- [ ] adapter passes ticket 0578's declaration-only contract checks
- [ ] shared assertions contain no zotero-mcp-specific branch
- [ ] every interface verb yields pass, fail, not-offered or not-run
- [ ] `make check` and `erg check tickets/` pass
